🤖 The last failure indicates that the Store.add method is modifying the Item instance passed in by the caller. The test expects the original item's qty to not change after adding it to the store and then adding more of the same item name.

In the add method currently:

```python
def add(self, item: Item) -> None:
    """Add stock. Items with the same name are merged. Must not modify the Item passed in."""
    if item.name in self.items:
        self.items[item.name].qty += item.qty
    else:
        self.items[item.name] = item
```

When we do self.items[item.name] = item, we are storing the original item instance, so further modifications affect it outside the store.

We should store a copy of the item to keep the original unchanged. Also, when merging the qty for existing items, we should not mutate the passed item but update the stored copy.

I will fix Store.add to copy the item before storing it if new, and only modify the stored item qty.
